 14	/**
 15	 * The compiled path's reading of a native binding.  A declaration whose body is
 16	 * exactly builtinPrimitive("pkg.Class.method"), the tight juxtaposition that walk's
 17	 * NativeApp.checkAndLoadNative recognizes, where the string names a public static
 18	 * method of a class of the helpers' package, com.sun.fortress.nativeHelpers., becomes
 19	 * a call of that method through the import java machinery: the component gains
 20	 * import java pkg.{Class.method => alias}, and the body becomes alias(args), the
 21	 * parameters in order, self first for a method of a trait or object (a dotted
 22	 * method's self added, a functional method's moved to the front), as walk's
 23	 * NativeMeth passes them.  Where the declaration gives an argument or the result
 24	 * the type NN32, NN64 or Char (Character in the compiler's prelude), and the helper's
 25	 * Java type there is an int or a long, which the checker reads as ZZ32 or ZZ64, that
 26	 * argument or the call goes through the matching one of the six transfer helpers,
 27	 * whose names the checker reads at the declared type (NamingCzar), as the prelude
 28	 * composes them: makeNN32FromZZ32(unsignedIntOverflowingAdd(makeZZ32FromNN32(self),
 29	 * makeZZ32FromNN32(b))); a position that the helper's own name already reads at the
 30	 * declared type, as each transfer's, gets none.  A declaration with a varargs
 31	 * parameter is left alone.
 32	 * A string under the helpers' package that names no public static method is a
 33	 * static error at the string.  Any other string is left alone, walk's glue classes
 34	 * ("pkg.Class$Op") among them, so that its body stays a call of builtinPrimitive.
 35	 *
 36	 * Shell.specificRepository turns it on for the compiled path's repository and off
 37	 * for walk's, which loads such a body itself.  Parser applies it to the parse of a
 38	 * component (parseFileConvertExn) and to the import collector's view of a component
 39	 * that names a helper (importCollector), so that the repository knows the foreign
 40	 * api when it builds its graph, before every phase.
